course: dictionary
lesson: 7442
title: Capital letters for places and peoples
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words start with a capital letter even in the middle of a sentence. Polynesian is one of them, because it names a place, Polynesia, and the peoples, languages and cultures that belong to it. «Polynesian navigators crossed the Pacific in double canoes.» Here Polynesian describes the navigators, so it is an adjective.
explain: When Polynesian means a person, it is a noun. «Several Polynesians taught the class about their voyages.» Here the word names people, so it is a noun. Polynesians is the plural, for more than one person.
explain: Use the context to decide which kind of word it is. If it describes something, it is an adjective. If it names a person, it is a noun. Try swapping in a word like "sailor" or "island" to check your idea.
fact: Polynesia is a large group of Pacific islands, including Hawaii, Samoa, Tonga, Tahiti and New Zealand (Aotearoa).
fact: As an adjective, «Polynesian» means to do with Polynesia, and with its peoples, languages and cultures.
fact: As a noun, «a Polynesian» means a person from one of these peoples, such as Māori, Samoan, Tongan or Hawaiian.
fact: «Polynesian sailors crossed thousands of kilometres of the Pacific Ocean in canoes, finding islands by reading the stars, the waves and the flight of birds.»
fact: Names of places, peoples and languages start with a capital letter, even in the middle of a sentence.
exercise: «Polynesian navigators sailed double canoes across the Pacific.» In this sentence, what kind of word is Polynesian? | *An adjective, because it describes the navigators | A verb, because it shows an action | A noun, because it names a person | A place name, because it names an ocean
exercise: What is Polynesia? | A big desert in Africa | *A large group of Pacific islands | A type of sailing boat | A river in Europe
exercise: Why does Polynesian start with a capital letter? | Because it is a very long word | Because it is the first word of every sentence | *Because it names a place and its peoples | Because it is a question
test: Which island is part of Polynesia? | Madagascar | Greenland | Iceland | *Samoa
test: «Polynesian navigators crossed the Pacific by reading the stars, the waves and the flight of birds.» What did the navigators use to find their way? | Radio signals from the land | Printed maps and a compass | Engines and fuel | *The stars, the waves and the flight of birds
exam: Which sentence uses Polynesian as a noun, meaning a person? | «Polynesian canoes were built with great skill.» | *«Several Polynesians taught the class about their voyages.» | «The Polynesian Triangle is marked on the map.» | «Polynesian dance is studied in many schools.»
